ProviderTest
├── rotate
│   ├── given a single item
│   │   └── it returns it unchanged
│   ├── given no items
│   │   └── it returns nothing
│   └── given several items
│       ├── it keeps every item
│       └── it starts somewhere else
├── fetchRates
│   ├── given the source is a specific provider
│   │   ├── it uses only that provider
│   │   └── given that provider fails
│   │       └── it does not fall back to the other one
│   ├── given the source is auto
│   │   ├── it does not always start with the same provider
│   │   ├── given the first provider it tries succeeds
│   │   │   └── it does not call the other one
│   │   ├── given the first provider it tries fails
│   │   │   ├── it falls back to the other one
│   │   │   └── it reports the first failure alongside the success
│   │   ├── given a provider returns an empty map
│   │   │   ├── it treats that as a failure
│   │   │   └── it falls back to the other one
│   │   ├── given a provider rejects with something that is not an Error
│   │   │   └── it still records a readable message
│   │   └── given every provider fails
│   │       ├── it reports failure
│   │       └── it reports every error
└── fetchRatesWithRetry
    ├── given the first attempt succeeds
    │   └── it does not retry
    ├── given an early attempt fails
    │   ├── it retries
    │   └── it backs off between attempts
    ├── given the transport is Nym
    │   ├── it retries fewer times
    │   └── it uses a flat backoff
    ├── when a retry count is given
    │   └── it overrides the transport default
    ├── given every attempt fails
    │   └── it returns the last result
    └── given a specific source
        └── it passes that source through to every attempt
